<section class="sec toolsec"><div class="wrap">
<div class="calc wide" data-tool="ready">
  <div class="calc-bar"><h2 class="calc-t">Appraisal readiness checkup</h2><span>10 questions · about two minutes</span></div>
  <div class="calc-grid">
    <div class="calc-in">
      <ol class="quiz"><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get coverage confirmed in writing. If the claim was denied outright, talk with a Kentucky attorney before thinking about appraisal."><span>Has the insurer accepted coverage for at least part of the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Ask the adjuster for the complete line-item estimate in writing."><span>Do you have the carrier’s full, itemized estimate — not just a summary page?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="3" data-fix="Get a line-item estimate. A one-line bid is hard to compare and easy to discount."><span>Do you have your own itemized estimate from a contractor or estimator?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Collect every photo, note the dates, and add photos of current conditions."><span>Do you have dated photos taken soon after the loss?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Look in the Conditions section of the policy and note any time limits."><span>Have you found and read the policy’s Appraisal paragraph?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Find the “Suit Against Us” clause and put the date on a calendar."><span>Do you know your policy’s suit-limitation date?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make reasonable temporary repairs and keep every receipt and invoice."><span>Were temporary repairs made, with receipts kept?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Make sure the full scope is visible before anyone prices it."><span>Has hidden damage (attic, decking, wall cavities) been opened up and documented?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="1" data-fix="Gather letters, emails and claim notes into one dated file."><span>Is your correspondence with the carrier saved in date order?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li><li data-w="2" data-fix="Run the appraisal payoff estimator. A small gap may not cover appraisal costs."><span>Is the gap more than about 10% of the carrier’s number or several thousand dollars?</span><span class="yn"><button type="button" class="yes" aria-pressed="false">Yes</button><button type="button" class="no" aria-pressed="false">No</button></span></li>
      </ol>
      <p><button type="button" class="btn line sm" data-reset>Reset answers</button></p>
    </div>
    <div class="calc-out" aria-live="polite">
      <p class="kpi"><small>Readiness score</small><b><span data-o="score">–</span><em>/100</em></b></p>
